  "id": "screwit",
  "neon": "#7dff6a",
  "note": "SCREW IT, the chemical supply on Ironside Street. A trade counter with a works behind it.\n\nThe plant is the building. What a chem supply is for happens above the parapet: the scrubber that\ntakes what comes off the drums, and the stack that puts the rest over the roofs. The stack is\ntaller than the scrubber because a fume stack has to clear everything near it, and on this street\nthat is the Embassy's shoulder two doors down.\n\nThe front is two halves under one lit canopy. On the left is the goods bay, a roller shutter\nbetween steel guard posts, where the drums go in and out. On the right is the shop: a display\nwindow on a stall riser and a glazed door between hazard-yellow posts with a striped kerb, an OPEN\nsign over it. Above the canopy runs the trade line, FASTENERS, SOLVENTS AND WHATEVER ELSE, and\nabove that the name in neon on a dark fascia (NEON_ART.screwit, client/shared/neon-signs.js): a\nslotted screw head in yellow whose slot turns a third at a time, SCREW IT in green, and a run of\nthread under it. The IT is on a bad circuit.\n\nA works doesn't sign itself (see UNSIGNED_TRADE); it carries a placard and a unit number. This one\nalso sells over a counter, which is the stated exception, so it carries both.",
  "pal": "ty_giardia",
